OL,4,CGovernment backs welfare shake-up to   
OL,5,Cprevent 'lost generation'              
OL,6,GThe government has backed plans by     
OL,7,Gformer minister Alan Milburn for       
OL,8,Gsweeping reforms to prevent "losing a  
OL,9,Ggeneration" of young people to a life  
OL,10,Gon benefits.                           
OL,12,FMilburn proposes spending billions on  
OL,13,Ftailored support for under 25s not in  
OL,14,Femployment, education or training      
OL,15,F(Neets), to be part-funded by cuts to  
OL,16,Fsome benefits.                         
OL,18,FHe claims his plan, which also         
OL,19,Fproposes tax breaks for firms and      
OL,20,Fmajor education reforms, will get      
OL,21,F440,000 young people into jobs by 2036.
